                    },
                    "message": "We could call the lightweight validation function here to skip emplacing any invalid configurations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/configuration.cpp",
                    "line": 163,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "You are setting `boardType` here but it has no effect in `postBoardToDBus` function since you are just writing to the local variable?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/configuration.cpp",
                    "line": 169,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Should this be `error` log?\n\nSince `Name` also has `error` log if it is not there."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/configuration.cpp",
                    "line": 171,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "From looking at `schemas/global.json`, `Type` and `Name` are required properties.\n\nSo i would suggest we can just skip these configurations altogether and not emplace them into `configurations` in the first place, instead of modifying the `configurations` collection later on.\n\nSince there is already the runtime json validation feature, maybe we can have a `validateJsonLight` function which just checks for the presence of\n\n`Name`, `Probe`, `Type`, `Exposes` properties as per `schemas/global.json`.\n\nThat way the validation is lightweight and we can still drop the check in `postBoardToDBus` function."
                }
            ],
